Linus, please pull from
	git://git.infradead.org/intel-iommu.git

This patchset improves the scalability of the Intel IOMMU code by
resolving two spinlock bottlenecks and eliminating the linearity of
the IOVA allocator, yielding up to ~5x performance improvement and
approaching iommu=3Doff performance.

Omer Peleg (8):
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0iommu/vt-d: refactoring of deferred flu=
sh entries
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0iommu/vt-d: per-cpu deferred invalidati=
on queues
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0iommu/vt-d: correct flush_unmaps pfn us=
age
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0iommu/vt-d: only unmap mapped entries
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0iommu/vt-d: avoid dev iotlb logic for d=
omains with no dev iotlbs
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0iommu/vt-d: change intel-iommu to use I=
OVA frame numbers
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0iommu/iova: introduce per-cpu caching t=
o iova allocation
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0iommu/vt-d: Use per-cpu IOVA caching

 drivers/iommu/intel-iommu.c | 318 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++=
+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------------------------=
----
 drivers/iommu/iova.c        | 417 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++=
+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++=
+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 include/linux/iova.h        |  23 ++++++++-
 3 files changed, 638 insertions(+), 120 deletions(-)

